  <content>
    <description>
      <levelledPara>
        <title>General</title>
        <para>The electrically driven cooling compressor (pre MOD-EWTW-021-001 configuration) is a two-stage centrifugal compressor on oil-free foil-gas bearings. It is the motive element of the electric environmental cooling unit of the eWTW green-native architecture (no engine bleed).</para>
      </levelledPara>
      <levelledPara>
        <title>Drive and control</title>
        <para>The compressor is driven by a 540 V DC permanent-magnet motor supplied from a remote motor controller installed in the forward equipment bay. The maximum continuous speed is 45 000 rpm; motor cooling is by ram-air through a dedicated cooling shroud.</para>
      </levelledPara>
    </description>
  </content>
